    "description": "Pyrite Sun Specimen\nNatural Iron Disulfide (Pyrite)\nSparta, Illinois Region\nThis natural Pyrite Sun, also historically referred to as a \"Miner's Dollar,\" features a distinct disc-like formation with a brilliant metallic brassy luster. These specimens are formed under extreme pressure between narrow layers of coal or shale, resulting in the unique radial growth pattern of acicular pyrite crystals extending from a central point. The formation captures light across its textured surface, highlighting the geometric precision of the mineral's growth habit.\nNatural Pyrite composition with characteristic golden metallic sheen\nUnique radial crystal habit forming a flat, circular \"sun\" shape\nOriginates from the Illinois coal mines, known for these specific formations\nDimensions: 3.25\" x 2.75\" x 0.25\"\nCondition:\nExcellent natural condition. The specimen maintains a strong metallic luster and structural integrity throughout. Radial edges are well-defined with typical natural irregularities. The surface shows distinct crystal growth lines with no major fractures or significant loss of the delicate outer edges. The specimen is flat and stable.\nOverall Condition\n: All items are USED and are sold AS-IS. Please open a ticket for any questions prior to bidding.\nUsed Item Description\n: Used condition indicates item(s) show signs of regular use, age and may have had repairs or may need repairs. All items featured are DONATED and all sales are FINAL. All BIDS are placed by the buyer with the understanding that this is a donated item that may contain faults unseen by our staff and is ultimately SOLD AS-IS as all information is presented. Items come strictly as pictured and should be assumed to be AS-IS with possible unseen defects. We are\nNOT\nexperts in any field.",
